// Filename:	MLPRO 2 Control PCB.test
// Project:		MLPRO 2
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    06.03.2024 Rev1
//
// Description: Tests the MLPRO 2 Control PCB
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
COMMENT: *Example image below*
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: ControlSetup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Setup equipment 1
a. Set the adjustable PSU output(1) to 12V ±0.1V, 1.5A ±0.1A and switch the output to off.
b. Set the adjustable PSU output(2) to 5V ±0.1V , 0.2 A ±0.1A and switch the output to off.
c. Using TE060, connect the PSU output(1) to FT1 & FT2 on the Control PCB. 
d. Using TE195, connect the PSU output(2) to X10 on the Control PCB.
COMMENT: *Example image below*
DISPLAY: ControlSetup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#3: Setup equipment 2
a. Connect the TE001 I/O Power button to J4 on the Control PCB.
b. Connect the PC (via Micro USB3 ) to the ML PRO 2 Control PCB (SK5 ).
c. On the PSU press the Output button for both PSU outputs.
d. Press the I/O Power button (TE001) to turn on the Control PCB.
DISPLAY: ControlSetup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2

#4: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  ENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  ENUM 

Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
IF: %ENUM% STR_EQ EEPROM,
GOTO: #4.1

IMPORTANT: This test has failed I2c is not working.
COMMENT: If you wish to move to next test, click fail to continue.
PASS_FAIL: #4
GOTO: #5

#4.1: PCB communication check 
TEST: PASSED
Result = Test Pass
CLICK_OK:

#5: PCB Program version check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BUILD
READLINE: MLPRO2  BUILD
IF:
Check the Returned result is current version as per TD037 PCB Programming Data Register.
.
..
...
Returned Version is = %BUILD%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . no communication
PASS_FAIL: #5

#6: Voltage check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  READVOLTS 
READLINE: MLPRO2  READVOLTS 
Returned Voltage is = %READVOLTS%

RANGE: %READVOLTS% 12000 50					// ASS if value is between a range
IF:											// IF a ture result the next line below actions
GOTO: #6.1: 								// if results match goto next test
IMPORTANT: This test has failed 
The expected result is =   between 12050 and 12150 // print this for test log information
PASS_FAIL: #6 								// Increments fail count and adds comment in log file
GOTO: #7
#6.1: Voltage check - test passed
TEST: PASSED
Result = Test Pass
CLICK_OK:								// Increments PASS count and adds comment in log file

#7: USB3 and USB2 ports test
a. Test K6 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB3 enumerated is displayed.
b. Test both ports on CONN6 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB2 enumerated is displayed. 
PASS_FAIL: #7

#8: Test complete:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BRESET
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
// End of file
